.TH CTBREC-VR-REMOTE 1 "2026-10-06" "ctbrec-vr-remote" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ctbrec-vr-remote \- run ctbrec-vr on the Proxmox server over ssh
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ctbrec-vr-remote
[\fIOPTIONS\fP]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ctbrec-vr-remote
is a thin local wrapper that runs
.BR ctbrec-vr (1)
on the Proxmox server. It connects with
.BR ssh (1)
(non\-interactive, no TTY, with the host's
.B RemoteCommand
disabled) and executes
.B /usr/local/bin/ctbrec-vr
with
.B \-\-dir /mnt/pve/Data_Storage/ctbrec
plus any arguments given to the wrapper.
.P
All scanning, probing, and moving happen on the server, where the recordings
live; nothing is transferred to the local machine. The remote interpreter runs
with
.B PYTHONUNBUFFERED\=1
so progress streams back live, and the remote exit status becomes the
wrapper's exit status.
.SH OPTIONS
All options are forwarded verbatim to
.BR ctbrec-vr (1);
see that page for the full list. The most useful are
.BR \-\-dry\-run ,
.BR \-\-age ,
and
.BR \-\-max\-moves .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CTBREC_VR_SERVER
Ssh host (or alias from
.BR ssh_config (5))
to run on. Defaults to
.BR proxmox .
.TP
.B CTBREC_VR_BIN
Path to the remote executable. Defaults to
.BR /usr/local/bin/ctbrec-vr .
.TP
.B CTBREC_VR_DIR
Remote recordings root passed as
.BR \-\-dir .
Defaults to
.BR /mnt/pve/Data_Storage/ctbrec .
.SH EXAMPLES
Preview what would move on the server:
.IP
.EX
ctbrec-vr-remote \-\-dry\-run
.EE
.P
Do a normal pass on the server:
.IP
.EX
ctbrec-vr-remote
.EE
.P
Move at most 20 files, ignoring I/O pressure:
.IP
.EX
ctbrec-vr-remote \-\-max\-moves 20 \-\-no\-io\-check
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
The exit status of the remote
.BR ctbrec-vr (1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ctbrec-vr (1),
.BR ctbrec-merge-remote (1),
.BR ssh (1)
